{{short description|Soup made with fish and oranges}}
'''Caldillo de perro''' (literally "dog soup") is a fish soup of [[Andalusia]] (southern [[Spain]]).<ref name="Fearnley-WhittingstallFisher2012">{{cite book|last1=Fearnley-Whittingstall|first1=Hugh|last2=Fisher|first2=Nick|title=The River Cottage Fish Book: The Definitive Guide to Sourcing and Cooking Sustainable Fish and Shellfish|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZwQBizVBm9oC|date=20 March 2012|publisher=Ten Speed Press|isbn=9781607740636|page=993}}</ref> The name is said to come from "el Perro," the nickname of a shipboard cook in [[El Puerto de Santa María]].<ref name="Ducasse2009">{{cite book|last=Ducasse|first=Alain|title=Gran libro de cocina de Alain Ducasse: Mediterráneo|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=JXLmj_2XmtwC&pg=PT268|date=13 November 2009|publisher=[[Ediciones Akal]]|language=Spanish|isbn=9788446023272|pages=268–269}}</ref>
The main ingredients are [[hake]], [[garlic]], [[olive oil]], [[lemons]], and [[Seville Orange|Seville oranges]].<ref name="Hopkinson2013">{{cite book|last=Hopkinson|first=Simon|title=Roast Chicken and Other Stories|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=4RyZAAAAQBAJ&pg=PT112|date=23 July 2013|publisher=Hyperion|isbn=9781401306144|page=112}}</ref> It is customarily served with sour [[orange juice]]. It is a common dish in the fishing districts.<ref name="Pérez2005">{{cite book|authorlink=Dionisio Pérez Gutiérrez|last=Pérez|first=Dionisio|title=Guía del Buen Comer Español|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ZB2V50CCjpEC&pg=PA94|date=4 November 2005|publisher=[[Editorial Maxtor]]|location=Madrid|language=Spanish|isbn=9788497612357|page=94}}</ref>
